{
    "name": "H-Bridge DC Motor Driver",
    "description": "A four-switch H-bridge driving a DC motor (modeled as a series R+L) with freewheel diodes. PULSE gate drives turn on opposite diagonals to reverse the current direction. Run a transient — the motor current reverses each half-period and the freewheel diodes conduct only at commutation. Uses generic LEVEL-1 MOSFETs (kΩ-scale Ron), so the absolute current is illustrative (a few mA). (Validated on ngspice.)",
